  "0": [
   {
    "context": "We've looked at it all, and the actual best, simplest answer is that Jesus resurrected. And they'll do this for lots of things. Again, all of a sudden, evidence matters, evidence becomes strong. Evidence is the differentiator between faiths. And that's wonderful. The problem is that many believers yo-yo between the two. If they get pushed on the abstract, they try to go to evidence. If they get pushed on evidence, they backtrack to the abstract. And many times they don't even see that they're doing it, and they just go to whichever way is more comfortable for them so they don't have to answer for the inconsistencies.",
    "dist": 0.3773,
    "occurrence_id": 146475,
    "published_at": "2026-06-14T14:00:07Z",
    "role": "host",
    "surface": "evidence",
    "t": 575.24,
    "title": "If Faith Proves Christianity, It Proves Every Religion",
    "video_id": "zLMpyoK-tds"
   },
   {
    "context": "So that's what I mean. And it's important, I think, first of all, to ask what scripture means by evidence. And that's why Jim here, and you can speak to this, Jim, and I like you to, is so concentrates on the evidence for the resurrection. Why I personally believe in the physical resurrection of Jesus. Things like Noah's Ark would be interesting if you could establish it accurately.",
    "dist": 0.3804,
    "occurrence_id": 22417,
    "published_at": "2023-12-29T18:09:35Z",
    "role": "host",
    "surface": "evidence",
    "t": 2517.24,
    "title": "John Lennox, William Lane Craig, and James Tour - Birthday Dinner Q&A",
    "video_id": "8tXvXO5GUw8"
   },
   {
    "context": "It's not scientific evidence by and large, it's historical evidence. But within any category of evidence, there is a spectrum of quality. The resurrection evidence is not the strong kind. Again, sadly, he will not elaborate, so we can't dig more deeply into what he's thinking. So that was one thing. And the other thing that came to me when I was uh at Cambridge, it became clear that Christianity ultimately is not, you know, some kind of moral theory or philosophy or something like that.",
    "dist": 0.3823,
    "occurrence_id": 72491,
    "published_at": "2026-06-26T13:30:35Z",
